-- 261 Shoreline Dr ---------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$399,000', beds='3', baths='2', sqft='1,433', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-07-21',
  description=$d$Your Sunny Hill Retreat! Sun from morning to evening, sweeping mountain views across the bay, and a beautifully updated log home in the heart of Seldovia. 3 bedrooms, 2 three-quarter baths, soaring vaulted ceilings, windows gathering the light from every direction, an expansive deck, workshop, and room to gather. This is Alaska living at its best.

Perched high on one of Seldovia's sunniest hillsides, this inviting home enjoys sunshine from morning until evening — a feature locals know is worth its weight in gold. From the expansive south-facing deck you'll enjoy ever-changing views overlooking the Seldovia Slough, peekaboo glimpses of Lake Susan, and sweeping vistas across Seldovia Bay to the surrounding mountains and rolling hills beyond. The deck quickly becomes your favorite place to be — morning coffee as the town wakes up, afternoons soaking in the sunshine, summer barbecues, or simply watching birds glide overhead. Surrounded by brilliant wild pink roses and mature raspberry bushes, the property feels both welcoming and peaceful.

Originally built in 1945, the home was extensively renovated in 2008 with care and craftsmanship: new windows, interior walls and trim, exposed beams, flooring, a beautifully remodeled kitchen, and numerous thoughtful updates. The exterior log walls were professionally restored and treated by a skilled log craftsman, preserving the warmth and character of the original home. Inside, soaring vaulted ceilings, warm wood accents, and abundant natural light fill an open-concept living area where family and friends naturally gather. Prepare meals on the gas range while conversation flows, enjoy dinner overlooking the views, or curl up beside the wood stove with a book. Two dependable heating stoves (living room and family room) add comfort through the seasons.

A generous family room is perfect for movie nights, crafts, a home office, game room, or guest quarters. Downstairs is another bedroom next to a spacious 3/4 bath with washer and dryer, plus an on-demand hot water heater for lingering warm showers. Upstairs, an open loft overlooks the living room; two bedrooms share a convenient bathroom with a walk-in shower. Outside, a large covered carport holds two vehicles end-to-end, and the detached workshop with electricity is ready for woodworking, hobbies, or storage. Even the crawl space is clean, spacious, well-lit, and easily accessible. Located in the center of town — minutes from the harbor, boardwalk, shops, restaurants, school, and community events — yet tucked away on your sunny hillside.

Highlights: Popular property · Bay view · Vaulted ceiling · Fronts an inlet · Hilly lot · Mud room.

Home details: Single Family · Built 1945 · 8,276 sq ft lot (waterfront, fronts an inlet) · Zoned RG (Residential General) · Log cabin, wood-frame construction, metal roof · Views of bay, lake, and city lights.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
where slug='261-shoreline-dr';

-- 3088 Jakolof Bay Rd ------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$515,000', beds='4', baths='3.5', sqft='2,966', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-07-21',
  description=$d$Evergreen Homestead — a private forest home in beautiful Seldovia. This well-built home was crafted by a master craftsman on a 3-acre site in a Sitka spruce forest, with an additional 684 sq ft one-bedroom cabin for guests or extended family. The main home offers 3 bedrooms, 2.5 baths (4 beds / 3.5 baths total with the cabin), a large kitchen, dedicated dining area, and vaulted ceilings with a cozy wood stove. Also included: a wood gazebo for wood storage and a 576 sq ft three-sided garage.

Nestled among roughly three acres of mature Sitka spruce, this custom home offers privacy, quality, and timeless character. A large fenced yard creates a wonderful outdoor space for children and pets while keeping Alaska's curious wildlife at a respectful distance. Peek-a-boo views of Kachemak Bay and the Homer Spit are a treat. Inside, warm wood finishes, soaring vaulted ceilings, and dramatic floor-to-ceiling picture windows invite the outdoors in. Morning sunlight pours into the living room as you enjoy coffee beside the wood stove or step onto the deck to watch the sunrise filter through the trees.

The spacious main level is designed for everyday living and entertaining: a kitchen with abundant cabinetry, a large island with bar seating, a built-in office nook, and a dedicated dining room that seats eight. The main-floor primary suite is a relaxing sanctuary with two walk-in closets and a private bath featuring dual sinks, a jetted soaking tub, and separate shower. A half bath near the entry welcomes guests, and a thoughtfully placed laundry room keeps household noise away from the living areas. Downstairs, a full basement provides abundant storage and workspace with easy access to utilities. Upstairs, an open landing makes a flexible bonus area, and two spacious bedrooms are connected by a Jack-and-Jill bath.

One of the property's most valuable features is a second home on site: a 684 sq ft one-bedroom with its own full kitchen, dining area, living room, three-quarter bath, and a private southwest-facing deck — ideal for extended family, a caretaker, a home office, or a vacation rental. A detached 576 sq ft three-sided garage provides covered parking, workshop space, and storage, plus a wood gazebo for your winter's wood supply. Accessible only by boat or airplane, Seldovia offers a rare sense of peace and community, with city services, high-speed internet, a K-12 school, medical clinic, grocery, restaurants, and regular ferry and air service to Homer.

Highlights: Hot property · Spa · Vaulted ceiling · Ocean view · Fronts a creek · Post and beam.

Home details: Single Family · Built 1998 · 3.03-acre lot (fronts a creek, level) · 1-car garage · Septic · Est. annual taxes $3,775 · Ocean & peek-a-boo views.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
where slug='3088-jakolof-bay-rd';

-- 230 Kachemak St ----------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$475,000', beds='3', baths='1.5', sqft='1,122', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-07-16',
  description=$d$A rare opportunity to own one of Seldovia's iconic waterfront properties. Set on approximately 0.20 acres — nearly four times the size of many neighboring lots — this historic Waterfront Commercial Residential property offers unmatched potential. This is an older home that has been remodeled; for the right buyer, it's a chance to preserve a piece of Seldovia's history while creating a lasting legacy.

Stretching along Seldovia's iconic waterfront, where the tides rise and fall beneath weathered pilings and fishing skiffs, this property has quietly been part of the town's story for decades. Its location alone couldn't be recreated today. Occupying roughly 0.20 acres of WCR-zoned land, it has served as both a family home and a commercial space. Inside, two main-floor bedrooms greet the morning with sunrise views across the slough, while upstairs a private guest retreat sleeps four with its own exterior entrance (and a half bath in the attic). Tucked above the downstairs bath, an unfinished attic hideaway offers one more cozy sleeping space.

The spacious kitchen — complete with two refrigerators — was made for gathering, with windows framing the quiet activity along Kachemak Drive. Just beyond, the generous living room opens through French doors to a deck of more than 400 square feet suspended above the slough, where you'll watch salmon move with the tide, fishermen cast from the bridge, and eagles pass overhead from one of the best seats in town.

This is a place with history — welcoming neighbors, visitors, and family as part of the daily rhythm of the waterfront. Few properties in Seldovia offer this combination of size, waterfront location, flexible zoning, and historical significance. The opportunities are as varied as the visions buyers bring: a distinctive private residence, guest accommodations, a gallery, boutique business, studio, or a blend of residential and commercial use. This is an older waterfront building and deserves an owner who understands what that means — expect to invest additional time, vision, and resources into its continued care. For the right person, that isn't simply maintenance; it's the privilege of preserving a place that has already stood the test of time.

Highlights: Hot property · Unobstructed views · Cabin · Fronts a lagoon/estuary · Shed.

Home details: Single Family · Built 1945 · 8,712 sq ft lot (fronts a lagoon/estuary) · Zoned WCR (Waterfront Commercial Residential) · Cabin, wood-frame, metal roof.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
where slug='230-kachemak-st';

-- 195 Lookout Aly ----------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$345,000', beds='2', baths='1.5', sqft='1,376', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-07-14',
  description=$d$Wake up to sunshine, slough, and harbor views from this welcoming corner-lot home in the heart of Seldovia. With 2 bedrooms, 1.5 baths, accessible entry ramps, sunny decks, berry gardens, a rustic workshop, and an easy walk to the harbor, shops, and restaurants, this property offers comfort, convenience, and the relaxed Alaska lifestyle.

Perfectly positioned on a sunny corner lot overlooking the Seldovia Slough, Main Street, and the harbor beyond, this 1,376 sq ft Lindal Cedar Home offers in-town living with peaceful views. Designed with accessibility in mind, it features 2 bedrooms, 1.5 baths, spacious living and dining areas, and ramps for easy access. Large windows invite natural light while offering glimpses of the surrounding trees, gardens, and neighborhood.

Step outside and discover a property ready to be enjoyed. Relax with morning coffee on the east-facing deck or evening sunshine on the west-facing harbor deck. Outdoor spaces on both sides of the home are surrounded by established gardens bursting with salmonberries and raspberries. A rustic 554 sq ft workshop is perfect for projects, hobbies, or storage. Located a short walk from the harbor, boardwalk, shops, restaurants, airport, post office, and community amenities, this home offers the best of small-town living with everything close at hand.

Highlights: Fronts an inlet · Private yard · Handicap accessible · Bay view · Fireplace · Outdoor storage · Decks on both sides · Established berry gardens · Mature trees for privacy.

Home details: Single Family (Lindal Cedar Home) · Built 1963 · 10,019 sq ft lot (waterfront, fronts an inlet, level, private yard) · Zoned WCR (Waterfront Commercial Residential) · Wood-frame, metal roof · Bay views.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
