-- 175 Augustine North Ave --------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$895,000', beds='7', baths='6', sqft='4,040', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-07-03',
  description=$d$A rare opportunity to own a 3,500+ sq ft home and waterfront cabin in the heart of Seldovia — 7 bedrooms, 6 baths, a successful turnkey B&B, oversized garage/shop, huge greenhouse, smokehouse, and nearly 90 feet of waterfront. Right in town, with breathtaking slough, bay, mountain, and sunset views, and endless residential or business potential.

Set in the heart of Seldovia with nearly 90 feet of waterfront along the slough, this 3,500+ sq ft home and waterfront cabin offers 7 bedrooms, 6 bathrooms, and a successful turnkey Bed & Breakfast. The iconic waterfront cabin is built right over the water, and there's also an oversized two-car garage and shop, a two-story greenhouse, a smokehouse, and one of the largest in-town waterfront settings along the slough. Waterfront land here is limited, and it's rare to find this much usable space — a large driveway with room for guests, boats, trailers, or RVs, plus the outbuildings, and still room to spread out. You're just three lots from the Seldovia Slough Bridge, an easy walk to the harbor, restaurants, shops, and airport.

The home was designed with guests in mind while feeling warm as a full-time residence. Upstairs are three beautifully furnished guest suites, each with a private 3/4 bath and sitting area, three with private decks. The main level centers on a vaulted two-story living room, a kitchen and dining nook, and a bright sunroom/formal dining area opening to a grand deck over the slough. Two additional main-floor guest rooms share the only tub bath. Downstairs offers a large bedroom, family room over the water, 3/4 bath, laundry, storage, and a dedicated fish-processing room with freezers.

Outside: a smokehouse with hot and cold smokers, an oversized 668 sq ft garage/shop, and an impressive two-story greenhouse with over 540 sq ft of growing space. The guest cabin, built on pilings over the water with a wraparound deck, enjoys nearly 180-degree slough views — the perfect spot for Songs On The Slough in July. Zoned Waterfront Commercial Residential, the property could continue as a B&B, become a family retreat, or simply be enjoyed as one of Seldovia's one-of-a-kind waterfront homes. Much of the furniture, furnishings, and equipment will remain (excluding personal items and select artwork).

Highlights: Fronts an inlet · Bay view · Mud room · Fronts a lagoon/estuary · Vaulted ceiling · Quartz countertops · Turnkey B&B.

Home details: Single Family · Built 1979 · 16,553 sq ft lot (waterfront) · Zoned WCR (Waterfront Commercial Residential) · 2-car attached garage · Cabin/wood-frame, metal roof · Lift-system sewer.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
where slug='175-augustine-north-ave';

-- 60187 Chesloknu Lease ----------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$425,000', beds='2', baths='0.5', sqft='1,631', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-06-07',
  description=$d$A rare waterfront opportunity on Seldovia Bay. This custom-built log home offers stunning bay, mountain, sunrise, and sunset views from a wraparound deck — and is accessible by private road, a unique feature for this side of the bay. Enjoy a spacious open-concept living area, large kitchen, beach access, and authentic off-grid Alaska living on a leased waterfront parcel with renewal options.

Built in 1988 by a local log craftsman, the home sits on the shoreline overlooking the head of Seldovia River and the sparkling waters of Seldovia Bay, catching both morning and afternoon sunshine. What truly sets it apart is private road access through Native lands — no other leased properties on this side of the bay offer this. Instead of arriving by boat and hauling supplies, you can drive right to your front door via the roughly 8,500-foot access road (not maintained in winter; owners plow or arrive by snow machine).

Inside, the home embraces classic Alaska living with a spacious kitchen, generous pantry, and propane appliances. Since electricity isn't available in this area, the home operates off-grid, with water hauled to two storage tanks. The open-concept living and dining area features vaulted ceilings and large windows framing views across the bay. The main-floor primary bedroom has large southwest-facing windows, and the wraparound deck offers nearly 180-degree vistas. Above the main level is an expansive loft of roughly 585 sq ft running the full length of the cabin, including a bright artist's atelier by the windows (counted as the second bedroom).

Wildlife is just outside your door — bald eagles, sea otters, and black bears along the shore, with thousands of pink salmon heading to the Seldovia River each summer. The home is offered fully furnished (excluding personal items, artwork, and a few sentimental pieces). The parcel is leased through the Seldovia Native Association under a 55-year lease expiring in 2042, with an option to renew for another 55 years (to 2097). 2025 lease was $3,587.63; 2025 taxes were $1,363.14.

Highlights: Fronts a bay or harbor · Bluff on lot · Wood countertops · Heated spa · Vaulted ceiling · Log cabin · Rare road access.

Home details: Single Family (log cabin) · Built 1988 · 3.18-acre leased lot · Not zoned · Off-grid (no electricity; hauled water) · Bay & unobstructed views · Sewer not available · Est. annual taxes $1,363.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
where slug='60187-chesloknu-lease';

-- 333 Anderson Way ---------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$300,000', beds='2', baths='1.5', sqft='1,120', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-06-07',
  description=$d$A heart-of-town opportunity! Three lots (0.69 acres total) across from Susan B. English School. A sun-filled 2 BR, 1.5 BA ranch with 1,120 sq ft, a spacious 768 sq ft shop, and a 256 sq ft shed. There's also space for an additional building, with city water, sewer, and power stubbed out. Walk anywhere in minutes. Sold as-is — ideal for town living and hobbies.

Imagine living where you can stroll to the harbor, wave to neighbors on the way to the grocery store, and enjoy community events minutes from your door — while still having nearly 0.69 acres to call your own. Situated on three town lots directly across from Susan B. English School, this property is a short walk from downtown shops, restaurants, the harbor, the Alaska Marine Highway dock, and the boardwalk.

The 1,120 sq ft ranch-style home offers comfortable single-level living with 2 bedrooms and 1.5 baths, and is bathed in natural light from sunrise over the mountains to the evening sun in the west. The property shines with its additional buildings: a spacious 768 sq ft shop for woodworking, boat projects, vehicle storage, or a home business, plus a 256 sq ft storage building — and room for an additional building with city water, sewer, and power already stubbed out. Zoned commercial, there are opportunities for business endeavors, gardens, outdoor entertaining, or simply breathing room. Offered as-is, this is an exceptional opportunity for someone with vision, whether you're after a full-time residence, a seasonal retreat, or an investment.

Highlights: Views · Ceiling fan · Level lot · Shed · Three lots (0.69 acres) · Zoned commercial · Utilities stubbed for an additional building.

Home details: Single Family · Built 1992 · 30,056 sq ft lot (level) · Zoned C (Commercial) · 2-car garage · Wood-frame, metal roof.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
