-- 251 Main St --------------------------------------------------------------
update public.listings set
  price='$685,000', beds='3', baths='3', sqft='2,240', status='For Sale', listed_on='2026-05-15',
  description=$d$A double lot on the Seldovia Small Boat Harbor! Morning sunrises and evening sunsets are yours, with the ONLY waterfront grassy lawn in town. This property boasts all kinds of possibilities: a spacious 2 bedroom / 2 bath home upstairs, a one-bedroom full-bath apartment downstairs, and a storefront on Main Street — plus a single-car garage/shop, a rare and useful asset on Main Street.

In the Commercial Business zone, steps from the bustling harbor and a stone's throw from shops, the airport, and all town amenities, this is your chance to craft a thriving business while living in coastal luxury upstairs. The Main Street-facing commercial space offers prime frontage — ideal for a gift shop, retail boutique, or professional office. On the waterfront side, a large patio leads to a fully furnished 1-bedroom apartment, perfect for a B&B or vacation rental, with a newly remodeled kitchen and bath, a cozy living room with a queen Murphy bed, and a covered patio with harbor views. All apartment furniture transfers with the sale, making it rental-ready from day one.

The surrounding lush grass yard — Seldovia's only large lawn on the harbor front — is a stunning backdrop for weddings, family gatherings, or waterfront entertainment, basking in sun from morning to sunset. The property sits in the heart of the community, between the Linwood Bar & Grill and the Boardwalk Hotel & Otter Cove Ice Cream, with the post office and grocery store right across the street.

Upstairs, your private oasis awaits with expansive harbor, mountain, and waterfront views from a large deck. The bright, open-concept living room flows into a chef's kitchen with solid-surface countertops, new appliances, modern lighting, and a grand island with a bar sink. An open dining area under vaulted ceilings, a cozy fireplace, two spacious bedrooms (including a water-side master with a fully remodeled 2023–2025 ensuite), a guest full bath, and a large pantry complete the retreat. Run your business below and escape the busy-ness of Main Street in this serene upstairs haven. The rare single-car garage and high-ceiling workshop is a game-changer for storing kayaks, bikes, a vehicle, ATVs, or creative projects. Some upstairs furnishings are negotiable; the seller's personal items, artwork, gift-shop merchandise, and golf-cart rental business are not included.

Highlights: Ocean view · Fronts a bay or harbor · Quartz countertops · Ocean access · Vaulted ceiling · Private yard · Live-work with storefront + apartment.

Home details: Single Family (mixed-use) · Built 1983 · 19,166 sq ft lot (fronts a bay/harbor, level, private yard) · Zoned CB (Commercial Business) · 1-car attached garage · Wood-frame + concrete block/stucco, metal roof · Ocean, bay, unobstructed, and city-light views.

Schools: Susan B. English Elementary & Middle School · Susan B. English High School.$d$
