$d$Sold July 29, 2026. A captivating one-bedroom cottage nestled in the vibrant heart of town — a haven brimming with eclectic, "cabiny" charm. An east-facing bay window bathes the main floor in soft morning light, and the living room's cozy reading nook begs you to sink in with a cup of tea. The kitchen is a true standout: a gleaming copper sink and handcrafted live-edge counters add rustic warmth, and a clever 3/4 bath maximizes the main floor.

Climb the staircase, framed by custom willow-wood railings, to an unexpectedly expansive master bedroom — spacious enough for a king bed with room to spare. Windows on the east, south, and west fill the room with light, and a window seat overlooking the wooded forest invites quiet reflection. Outside, the landscaped yard bursts with rhubarb, raspberries, salmonberries, and strawberries, with magpies, jays, squirrels, bunnies, and the occasional black bear visiting the gardens. The sunny deck catches early rays — perfect for morning coffee or evening gatherings. A garden shed and lean-to store tools and host a washer, and there's ample parking for a car, 4-wheelers, or a boat.

Tied into city water, sewer, and reliable HEA power, this cottage is as practical as it is enchanting — steps from local shops, restaurants, the post office, harbor, school, and airport.

Home details: Single Family (cabin) · Built 1978 · 6,534 sq ft lot (waterfront, level, private yard) · Zoned RG (Residential General) · Wood-frame, metal roof · Sold at $293/sq ft after 5 days on market.

